cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Who's Harry Potter? An interactive walk through approximate
  unlearning in LLMs
message: >-
  If you use this notebook or its code in your own work, please
  cite it as below. The original research paper being explained
  has its own citation; see the references section.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jacob
    family-names: Bowie
    email: jacob.bowie2@gmail.com
    affiliation: University of Connecticut
abstract: >-
  An interactive marimo notebook explaining Eldan & Russinovich's
  2023 paper "Who's Harry Potter? Approximate Unlearning in LLMs."
  The headline visualization frames the unlearning mechanism as
  edge surgery on the model's knowledge graph: the algorithm
  removes specific learned associations between entities while
  leaving the surrounding language graph intact. Runs entirely in
  the browser via Pyodide.
